    "result_text": "All 262 tests pass, including the new email-duplicate test. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the change in the V1 owner creation endpoint (`addOwner`) in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`. When a request supplies an email, after it's normalized (trimmed, lower-cased), the controller now checks all existing owners and returns **409 Conflict** if any other owner already uses the same email (compared case-insensitively):\n\n```java\nowner.setEmail(email);\nfor (Owner existing : this.clinicService.findAllOwners()) {\n    if (existing.getEmail() != null && email.equalsIgnoreCase(existing.getEmail())) {\n        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis follows the existing conventions in the file (the same `findAllOwners()` iteration pattern already used for the telephone-duplicate and city-capacity checks). The check sits after email validation, so an invalid email still yields 400 as before.\n\nI also added a test, `createOwnerDuplicateEmailReturnsConflict`, that creates an owner with `George.Mailer@Example.com` and confirms a second creation with `george.mailer@example.com` (differing only in case) is rejected with 409. The full suite \u2014 262 tests \u2014 is green.",
